# Phase 3 remoting transport execution log

- Date/session: 2026-09-26 UTC, `20260926T094303Z`.
- Scope: continue Phase 3 parity review, focused on RPC hooks; Java RocketMQ 5.5.1 source in `/Users/nanashi07/Projects/3rd/rocketmq/remoting/` is read-only oracle. Phase plans unchanged; Phase 4 remains blocked.
- Source findings: Java hook loops invoke hooks directly (no local catch) in outbound async/future/oneway and inbound handlers; Java `invokeSync` calls `invokeSyncImpl` and skips hooks. Hook errors are therefore not ignored on outbound paths. Inbound handler converts ordinary hook exceptions to its SYSTEM_ERROR path, continues the documented before-hook/pipeline/after ordering, while `AbortProcessException` produces abort response. Registration uses `List.contains`, hence existing-hook `equals` semantics.
- Changes: outbound sync-future/async before+after hook result failures now map to `TransportError::RpcHook` instead of being silently discarded; async callback receives the failure through callback result. One-way stops before marking/admission/send when a fallible before hook fails (there is no post-return result channel). Outbound hook panic is no longer caught, so task panic follows the runtime boundary instead of silently continuing. Inbound catch/response mapping remains. `RpcHook::equality_key` optionally supports equals-style registration deduplication, with identity still deduped by default. Java mutable public hook-list inspection/removal remains a known gap.
- Tests: added `p3_outbound_hook_failures_are_not_ignored` to check sync-future, callback, and after-hook errors; added `p3_rpc_hook_equality_keys_match_java_contains_semantics`; adapted existing duplicate test to register distinct instances with matching keys. Targeted tests passed, then all 58 transport tests passed.
- Documentation: compatibility matrix, detailed inventory, ADR, and README updated; no plan edits.
- Validation PASS: `cargo fmt --all --check`; `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked --offline -- -D warnings`; `cargo test --workspace --locked --offline` (11 common, 9 protocol, 13 remoting unit, 4 codec, 58 transport tests; doc-tests pass); `python3 scripts/check-workspace-metadata.py`; `python3 tests/differential/compare.py --self-test`; `git diff --check`.
- Not run: Java Maven, Docker/live Broker. P3-V04 remains Phase 19.
- Phase 3 remains NOT ACCEPTED. Remaining blockers include broader public config/API semantics, TLS property/key lifecycle, executor/event behavior, full error/timeout races, Netty-native-equivalent capabilities and NameServer/channel-wrapper lifecycle. No parity claim.
- Commit status: code, tests, docs and this append-only session log are pending separate commits after review.
